gaaF(){return"Updated on October 29, 2026."},
gaan(){return"Mirinu is a personal project by Marco, in Switzerland. He is responsible for the data described here. For any question: contact@mirinu.ch."},
gaav(){return"On your device"},
gaao(){return"Mirinu has no account and asks for neither your name nor your email address. Your library, your ratings and your settings stay on your device: in the app on Android, in the browser's storage on app.mirinu.ch, without cookies. A file you import is read on the spot and sent nowhere."},
gaal(){return"On Android, if your phone's Google backup is on, it may copy your library, as it does for your other apps."},
gaar(){return"No ads, no trackers, no audience measurement."},
gaaw(){return"What leaves your device"},
gaas(){return"To show a title page or recognize the titles of an import, the app sends the title or number searched for to TMDB and MangaUpdates, directly or through the Mirinu relay. Images come from their servers, fonts and trailer thumbnails from Google's. These services see your IP address, like any website, and follow their own rules."},
gaaq(){return"The \u201cHelp improve matching\u201d setting, on at first, sends the relay the two numbers of an entry you pick during an import, with nothing that identifies you. You can turn it off in the settings."},
gaaz(){return"Sync and security"},
gaaE(){return"If you link several devices, your library is encrypted on your device before it is sent to the relay. The relay only keeps data it cannot read, and the key never goes through it in the clear."},
gaaB(){return"If you find a security flaw, write to contact@mirinu.ch before making it public."},
gaat(){return"With an account"},
gaah(){return"The account is only for people aged 15 or over. It lets you get your library back if you lose your device, and manage your devices from any browser. Like sync, it serves the service you ask for."},
gaaj(){return"The relay keeps your email address, encrypted; if you sign in with Google, an unreadable identifier of your Google account and its address, encrypted. It also keeps the list of your devices (type and dates, to the day) and your encrypted library, which it cannot read. Your recovery code never leaves your devices."},
gaai(){return"Sign-in codes and security notices are sent from contact@mirinu.ch, through Infomaniak (Switzerland). Mirinu never writes to advertise. If you sign in with Google, Google knows that you use Mirinu; Google adheres to the Data Privacy Framework."},
gaag(){return"A sign-in code is valid for 10 minutes. Account data stays as long as the account exists. You can delete it whenever you want: it is erased 7 days after your request, then leaves the relay's backups within 7 more days. An account inactive for 24 months is erased, after a warning email."},
gaax(){return"Providers and countries"},
gaaA(){return"Cloudflare (United States, servers in several countries) runs the relay. On the website, manga and novel searches and pages also go through Vercel (United States), without your IP address or anything that identifies you. GitHub (United States) hosts mirinu.ch and app.mirinu.ch, and keeps its own access logs. Infomaniak (Switzerland) hosts the contact@mirinu.ch mailbox. Cloudflare, Vercel and GitHub take part in the Data Privacy Framework, which Switzerland and the EU recognize for data sent to the United States."},
gaau(){return"Legal bases and retention"},
gaam(){return"Mirinu follows the Swiss data protection act and, for people in the EU, the GDPR. Sync and showing title pages serve the service you ask for (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR). Matching and hosting rest on the legitimate interest in running the service (Art. 6(1)(f))."},
gaap(){return"Mirinu does not keep your IP address. The relay erases a synced copy 180 days after its last sync. An email you send is kept while your request is handled."},
gaay(){return"Your rights"},
gaaC(){return"You can find out what Mirinu keeps about you, have it corrected or erased, receive it in a file, object to a processing or have it restricted. Write to contact@mirinu.ch: the answer comes within 30 days. Your library can be exported from the app, and the \u201cDelete your data\u201d page explains how to erase everything."},
gaak(){return"You can also contact the Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC) or, in the EU, the authority of your country."},
gaci(){return"Updated on October 29, 2026."},
gac5(){return"Mirinu is a free app, made by Marco in Switzerland. By using it, you accept these terms. Contact: contact@mirinu.ch."},
gacd(){return"The service"},
gacg(){return"Mirinu is provided as is, without warranty. The relay may be slow, down or shut down; your library then stays usable on your device. Mirinu may change or stop."},
gacc(){return"Your library"},
gac8(){return"It belongs to you and stays on your device. Keep an export (Export my data) somewhere other than your phone: without sync or an export, a library lost with the device cannot be recovered."},
gace(){return"Title information"},
gach(){return"Posters, synopses and dates come from TMDB and MangaUpdates, which keep the rights to them. Mirinu uses TMDB and its APIs but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB."},
gacf(){return"Fair use"},
gacj(){return"The relay is for Mirinu and nothing else. Do not try to overload it or to use it from another program: abusive use may be blocked."},
gac9(){return"The account"},
gac3(){return"You must be 15 or over to create an account. Keep your recovery code yourself: Mirinu does not know it and cannot recover it. If you lose all your devices and this code, nobody can reopen your library."},
gac4(){return"You can delete your account whenever you want. An account inactive for 24 months is erased, after a warning email."},
gacb(){return"Liability"},
gac7(){return"Marco is not liable for damage caused by an outage, an interruption or a loss of data, except in case of gross negligence or intent. The rules that protect consumers in your country remain unaffected."},
gaca(){return"Governing law"},
gac6(){return"These terms are governed by Swiss law. The Privacy page explains what Mirinu does with your data."},
ga8h(){return"Delete your data"},
ga8i(){return"Updated on October 28, 2026."},
ga87(){return"Mirinu has no account. Your data is on your devices and, if you use sync, in an encrypted copy on the Mirinu relay."},
ga89(){return"On Android"},
ga85(){return"Uninstall Mirinu. To keep the app and start over: in Android's settings, open Apps, then Mirinu, Storage, and clear the storage. Exports you saved elsewhere remain: delete them yourself. A copy kept by your phone's Google backup is managed in that backup's settings."},
ga8a(){return"In the browser"},
ga86(){return"In your browser's settings, clear the site data of app.mirinu.ch. Your library disappears from that browser."},
ga8c(){return"The sync copy"},
ga8e(){return"On each linked device, open Sync, in Profile on a phone or in Settings on a computer."},
ga8f(){return"Choose \u201cStop sync on this device\u201d."},
ga8g(){return"Once no device syncs anymore, the relay erases the encrypted copy after 180 days. It cannot read it and does not know who it belongs to."},
ga88(){return"Your account"},
ga84(){return"If you have an account, delete it in the app (Account and sync, Delete my account) or at app.mirinu.ch/#/supprimer, without installing the app. Your account and your encrypted library are erased from the relay 7 days after your request; until then, you can cancel. What is on your devices stays there."},
ga8b(){return"A question"},
